error[E0405]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), which can't be put in a cown
  --> cown_resource.ck:11:5
   |
11 |     cown.new f s
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: `f` is passed to `cown.new`; a cown's handle can be shared, so nothing would make sure what it holds is closed
   = help: keep the resource with one owner, passing it on through calls, `fork` and `join`; a cown may hold the rest of the state

error[E0405]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), which can't be put in a cown
  --> cown_resource.ck:18:5
   |
18 |     cown.new (Job f 0) s
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: `f` is passed to `cown.new`; a cown's handle can be shared, so nothing would make sure what it holds is closed
   = help: keep the resource with one owner, passing it on through calls, `fork` and `join`; a cown may hold the rest of the state

error[E0405]: `v` is `own`, so it may be a resource, which can't be put in a cown
  --> cown_resource.ck:21:5
   |
21 |     cown.new v s
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: remove `own`: a cown holds only values that aren't resources

error[E0405]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), which can't be put in an actor's state
  --> cown_resource.ck:24:5
   |
24 |     actor.new (Some f) s
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: `f` is passed to `actor.new`; a cown's handle can be shared, so nothing would make sure what it holds is closed
   = help: keep the resource with one owner, passing it on through calls, `fork` and `join`; a cown may hold the rest of the state

